[gd_scene format=3]

; The LIGHT-PED body -- the far tier of the ambient crowd (PedCrowd, PLAN.md 3.6d), built by
; blender/tools/build_ped_body.py from the SHIPPED shino.glb.
;
; It is shino.tscn's job with one surface instead of seventeen: at PedCrowd's nearest draw distance
; (promoteDistance, 80 m) a 1.65 m body is ~14 px tall, so what costs anything there is DRAW CALLS.
; One atlas, one material, one skinned mesh, and only the two clips PedCrowd plays.
;
; Like shino.tscn it exists to state the armature's 180-degree turn: a VRoid export faces +Z while
; the game faces -Z (W41, "the armature's frame is not the game's"), and a crowd that writes walk
; transforms onto an unturned body walks backwards.

[ext_resource type="PackedScene" path="res://assets/characters/shino/shino_ped.glb" id="1_shino_ped"]

